5. TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE

Use a modern, modular, production-oriented architecture.

Preferred stack

Frontend:

- React.
- TypeScript.
- Next.js if supported reliably by the selected Google AI Studio Build environment; otherwise use its supported React application setup.
- Tailwind CSS.
- A consistent reusable component system.
- Accessible, responsive UI.

Backend:

- Node.js.
- TypeScript.
- Secure server-side API routes.
- Service and repository layers.
- Input validation.
- Structured error handling.
- Authentication and authorization middleware.

Database:

- PostgreSQL.
- Supabase is the preferred managed PostgreSQL platform.
- Supabase Auth where appropriate.
- Supabase Storage for uploaded documents and generated files.
- Row Level Security.
- Database migrations committed to source control.

Do not use browser-only local storage as the main database.

Do not choose Firestore simply because it is easy to provision. This application requires relational data, joins, reporting, and strong tenant isolation. If Google AI Studio offers Firebase integration automatically, do not enable Firestore as the primary application database without discussing the trade-off first.

AI:

- Gemini API for appropriate AI workflows.
- A provider abstraction that allows additional AI providers in the future.
- Structured JSON outputs.
- Tool/function calling where appropriate.
- Server-side model calls only.

Background processing:

- Inngest or Trigger.dev.
- Scheduled jobs.
- Durable background tasks.
- Retries.
- Idempotency.
- Concurrency limits.
- Usage tracking.

Deployment:

- Google Cloud Run or another suitable production hosting environment.
- GitHub for source control.
- Environment variables and secrets management.
- Separate development, staging, and production environments.

Analytics:

- PostHog or an equivalent privacy-conscious product analytics service.

Important: verify the actual compatibility and current documentation of every selected library and service before implementation.

Create a modular architecture so individual providers can be replaced without rewriting the application.

